      "content": "okay, thanks for the clarification. i'll keep looking into the valve plates and spools.\n\nbut honestly, going back to that \"mischievous\" part—it's really bothering me because it's so hard to pin down. it's like there's some tiny, unseen interference that's causing these millisecond-long surges and then just vanishing. \n\nis there anything else that could cause a \"phantom\" surge like that? something that doesn't leave a physical trace like a broken part or a clog, but just causes a sudden, momentary chaos in the pressure?",
